Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for SSH2 and SFTP
=======================================

qore-ssh2-module contains native SSH2/SFTP bindings, compiled/source
SftpClientDataProvider, SftpPollerUtil, SftpPoller and Ssh2Connections modules,
compiler metadata, resources and translations. The doc package contains five
HTML references and all example tests; debhelper creates detached debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native environment with the packaged Qore runtime/SDK and
Build-Depends from debian/control. The qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04
amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages. Other releases/architectures need a
matching SDK and native qualification. Cross builds are rejected because Qore,
qpp and qcc execute during compilation/documentation. The sshutil module is
bundled with the required Qore runtime. System libssh2/OpenSSL are required;
no SSH or cryptographic implementation is bundled.

The build uses distribution hardening flags and qcc debug information. Fixed
QCC_JOBS=1 makes partitioning independent of jobserver load while independent
targets remain parallel. A dh_strip wrapper preserves dependency, optional-module
and source-location trailers. dwz is disabled for AOT objects because of LLVM
DWARF support limitations. Runtime/libqore SONAME dependencies derive from the
installed SDK; other libraries use dh_shlibdeps. The native package is not
Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native interpreter.

Isolated integration tests
--------------------------

Tests start an unprivileged OpenSSH server on a temporary loopback port with
fresh host/client keys, public-key-only authentication and internal SFTP.
libnss-wrapper gives the test user a temporary home for libc account lookups,
including the driver's default known_hosts path. No system account or existing
SSH files are modified. The SFTP provider test accepts an explicit URI, so file
operations target the temporary directory. The helper removes its server/keys
and home on exit and bounds the suite group to ten minutes. Modern OpenSSH
per-source penalties are disabled in this isolated server to allow deliberate
negative authentication tests without delaying later valid connections.

OpenSSH and nss_wrapper are test-only dependencies, absent from the runtime
package. Build and installed tests use the exact compiled modules. Source-mode
qualification runs separately. A connection preflight prevents silently skipped
integration tests. All connection traffic stays on the container's loopback;
build/test containers have no external network access.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a new version for each changed upload. This snapshot precedes version 2.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=2.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../ssh2-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-ssh2-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../ssh2-package-work/qore-ssh2-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../ssh2-package-work/qore-ssh2-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../ssh2-package-work
    cp -a debian "../ssh2-package-work/qore-ssh2-module-$version/"
    cd "../ssh2-package-work/qore-ssh2-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x. With dependencies preinstalled, build
unprivileged with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) need no Doxygen; independent builds (-A) produce
HTML documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc
suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc package. Do not use
nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

Run all eight suites in build/installed/source modes, a fresh qcc executable
using native named arguments and the provider factory, AOT trailer/resource
parity and complete standard-locale checks. Check Lintian, hardening/debug
symbols, installation without the SDK or SSH server, docs/debug coinstallation,
dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and reproducibility at different paths/job counts.
Retain source/package hashes, dependency versions, audit and test logs.
Testing PPA publication is separate from approval for a final general release.
